# Patch 0001 — Add fusion_cas knowledge layer to AI-Q (v2)
#
# Source of truth: blog post "Connecting IBM Fusion CAS to NVIDIA AI-Q on OpenShift - v2"
#
# Files patched:
#   sources/knowledge_layer/pyproject.toml     — package list + optional-dep group
#                                                (Python-based, done by inject_pyproject() in 01-patch-aiq.sh)
#   sources/knowledge_layer/src/register.py    — 4 additions (described below)
#
# Key v2 differences from v1:
#   - Adapter is adapter.py (multi-store + source_id_store_map + enabled_source_ids)
#   - Addition 4 reads _active_data_sources context var and passes enabled_source_ids to retriever
#   - pyproject.toml changes are identical to v1
#
# ── KNOWN GAP: _active_data_sources.set() must be called by the agent layer ──
#
# register.py declares _active_data_sources (a ContextVar) and search_nat reads
# it via .get() to decide which stores to fan out to.  However the .set() call
# must happen in the chat_deepresearcher_agent / chat_researcher_agent workflow,
# just before ainvoke() is called on the agent graph — otherwise the ContextVar
# is always None and the retriever ignores UI data-source selection.
#
# Symptom: knowledge_search always queries ALL configured stores regardless of
# which fusion_cas_N toggle the user enabled in the Data Sources panel.
# The agent still works (returns results) but does not respect per-store selection.
#
# Fix location: aiq_agent/agents/chat_researcher/agent.py (or the register for
# chat_deepresearcher_agent) — wherever `ainvoke` / `astream` is first called.
# Add, just before the graph call:
#
#   from knowledge_layer.register import _active_data_sources
#   token = _active_data_sources.set(list(state.data_sources or []))
#   try:
#       result = await self._graph.ainvoke(state, config=config)
#   finally:
#       _active_data_sources.reset(token)
#
# The data_sources field is already present in the request payload (confirmed
# in nat.builder.function:211 error log: data_sources=['web_search','fusion_cas_1','fusion_cas_2']).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

